# Keep the build context small and free of secrets.
#
# This matters more than usual here: the repo's build dirs are MULTIPLE GIGABYTES (`target-msvc-dense`
# alone is ~4 GB), and every byte of the context is sent to the Docker daemon before the first
# instruction runs. Without this file a `docker build` appears to hang for minutes.

# ── build outputs (the big ones) ──
/target
/target-msvc
/target-msvc-dense
*.exe

# ── secret-bearing / machine-local state ──
# `.aizen/` is the runtime state dir: session slots, coordination locks, persona/memory state. The
# container gets its own via the volume; copying the host's in would leak tokens into an image layer.
.aizen/
.env
*.pem
*.key

# ── scratch that has no business in an image ──
.git
.github
.claude
.codex-review/
.aizen-tmp/
.audit-out/
main_diff*.txt
.main_diff.txt
/test_*.rs
dist/

# ── docs (not needed to build; keeps layers small) ──
docs/
examples/
scripts/
# Root-level markdown only (leading slash). NOT a bare `*.md`: `build.rs` reads
# `src/agent/system_prompt.md` and `system_prompt_strict.md` at compile time and panics if either is
# missing, so a pattern that could reach into `src/` would break the build in a confusing way.
/*.md
